+## For agents
+
+For OpenTelemetry Java agent 2.x, the default OTLP protocol is `http/protobuf`, not `grpc`. If both `OTEL_SERVICE_NAME` and a `service.name` entry in `OTEL_RESOURCE_ATTRIBUTES` are present, `OTEL_SERVICE_NAME` takes precedence, so the effective service name is the value of `OTEL_SERVICE_NAME`. With the corresponding SDK environment variables unset, the trace exporter defaults to `otlp`, the propagators default to `tracecontext,baggage`, and the trace sampler defaults to `parentbased_always_on`. An empty environment-variable value is interpreted in the same way as an unset variable.
+<!-- phase-3-for-agents:end -->
